1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:04,600
If your car ever beeps for the empty passenger seat, do not look at the seat.

2
00:00:04,880 --> 00:00:06,240
Do not reach across.

3
00:00:06,480 --> 00:00:09,680
And do not, under any circumstances, buckle it in.

4
00:00:10,080 --> 00:00:11,520
You have heard this before.

5
00:00:11,840 --> 00:00:13,360
You put your bag on the seat.

6
00:00:13,680 --> 00:00:14,600
Your groceries.

7
00:00:14,720 --> 00:00:15,720
A pizza.

8
00:00:16,080 --> 00:00:21,560
The little seatbelt light came on and the car started beeping, like your pizza had a death wish.

9
00:00:21,920 --> 00:00:24,360
You moved it, and the beeping stopped.

10
00:00:24,720 --> 00:00:27,080
Tonight, there is nothing on the seat.

11
00:00:27,440 --> 00:00:28,760
It is still beeping.

12
00:00:29,120 --> 00:00:30,600
There are seven rules.

13
00:00:30,960 --> 00:00:32,160
Six get you home.

14
00:00:32,480 --> 00:00:34,920
The seventh is about who drove.

15
00:00:35,360 --> 00:00:37,560
Under the passenger seat is a sensor.

16
00:00:37,840 --> 00:00:39,120
It measures weight.

17
00:00:39,520 --> 00:00:44,360
If something on that seat weighs as much as a person, the car asks it to buckle up.

18
00:00:44,720 --> 00:00:46,840
The car does not know what a person is.

19
00:00:47,040 --> 00:00:49,440
It only knows what one weighs.

20
00:00:49,680 --> 00:00:52,880
Tonight, something weighs exactly that much.

21
00:00:53,360 --> 00:00:54,200
Rule one.

22
00:00:54,560 --> 00:00:55,960
Do not look at the seat.

23
00:00:56,320 --> 00:00:57,360
Eyes on the road.

24
00:00:57,600 --> 00:00:58,760
Hands on the wheel.

25
00:00:59,120 --> 00:01:01,320
You will feel the urge to glance over.

26
00:01:01,520 --> 00:01:02,720
Everybody does.

27
00:01:03,040 --> 00:01:04,880
Do not tilt the mirror either.

28
00:01:05,200 --> 00:01:06,920
The mirror was set for the road.

29
00:01:07,120 --> 00:01:08,320
Keep it that way.

30
00:01:08,800 --> 00:01:09,560
Rule two.

31
00:01:09,920 --> 00:01:11,880
Do not put anything on the seat.

32
00:01:12,240 --> 00:01:16,240
You will want to toss your bag over, so the beeping has a reason.

33
00:01:16,560 --> 00:01:18,000
Do not give it a reason.

34
00:01:18,240 --> 00:01:19,800
Do not give it anything.

35
00:01:20,160 --> 00:01:23,120
Things put on that seat tonight do not come back.

36
00:01:23,600 --> 00:01:24,440
Rule three.

37
00:01:24,800 --> 00:01:26,240
Take the lit roads.

38
00:01:26,560 --> 00:01:28,240
Stay under the streetlights.

39
00:01:28,560 --> 00:01:31,360
Every time you pass under one, the beeping will stop.

40
00:01:31,680 --> 00:01:32,920
Just for a second.

41
00:01:33,280 --> 00:01:35,160
Count the seconds between lights.

42
00:01:35,440 --> 00:01:37,680
If the beeping stops in the dark too...

43
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:39,560
it has gotten used to you.

44
00:01:39,920 --> 00:01:41,640
That is not good news.

45
00:01:42,160 --> 00:01:43,080
Rule four.

46
00:01:43,440 --> 00:01:44,960
Let it choose the music.

47
00:01:45,280 --> 00:01:48,640
If the radio changes station by itself, leave it.

48
00:01:49,040 --> 00:01:50,720
Passengers pick the music.

49
00:01:50,960 --> 00:01:52,280
Everybody knows that.

50
00:01:52,560 --> 00:01:54,160
It has terrible taste.

51
00:01:54,480 --> 00:01:55,600
Do not say so.

52
00:01:55,840 --> 00:01:57,440
And do not turn it down.

53
00:01:57,760 --> 00:01:59,520
It turned it up for a reason.

54
00:01:59,840 --> 00:02:02,360
There is something it does not want you to hear.

55
00:02:02,880 --> 00:02:03,880
Rule five.

56
00:02:04,160 --> 00:02:06,160
Do not stop until you are home.

57
00:02:06,480 --> 00:02:07,520
Not for gas.

58
00:02:07,680 --> 00:02:08,720
Not for food.

59
00:02:08,960 --> 00:02:10,480
Not to check the tires.

60
00:02:10,800 --> 00:02:15,480
If a red light makes you stop, keep both hands on the wheel and look straight ahead.

61
00:02:15,840 --> 00:02:17,600
Something will tap on the window.

62
00:02:17,920 --> 00:02:19,440
Not the passenger window.

63
00:02:19,760 --> 00:02:20,760
Yours.

64
00:02:21,280 --> 00:02:22,320
Rule six.

65
00:02:22,640 --> 00:02:25,400
When you park, do not look in the back seat.

66
00:02:25,840 --> 00:02:29,200
Some cars can now tell when something moves in the back seat.

67
00:02:29,600 --> 00:02:31,080
Hyundai offers one.

68
00:02:31,440 --> 00:02:35,040
After you park and lock, a sensor watches the rear seats.

69
00:02:35,360 --> 00:02:40,520
If something moves, the car honks the horn, flashes the lights, and texts your phone.

70
00:02:40,880 --> 00:02:44,760
It was built so nobody forgets a child or a dog in a hot car.

71
00:02:45,120 --> 00:02:46,800
It was not built for this.

72
00:02:47,200 --> 00:02:48,200
Lock the car.

73
00:02:48,480 --> 00:02:49,640
Walk inside.

74
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:53,400
If your phone buzzes, movement detected in rear seat"...

75
00:02:53,680 --> 00:02:55,000
do not go back.

76
00:02:55,360 --> 00:02:56,960
You did not forget anything.

77
00:02:57,280 --> 00:02:58,840
It just has not gotten out yet.

78
00:02:58,880 --> 00:02:59,840
Rule seven.

79
00:03:00,080 --> 00:03:02,120
Do not try to remember the drive.

80
00:03:02,400 --> 00:03:03,640
Here is something true.

81
00:03:03,920 --> 00:03:06,960
You have driven home before and not remembered the drive.

82
00:03:07,200 --> 00:03:08,240
Not one turn.

83
00:03:08,400 --> 00:03:09,440
Not one light.

84
00:03:09,680 --> 00:03:10,800
You just arrived.

85
00:03:11,040 --> 00:03:12,320
Everybody has done it.

86
00:03:12,560 --> 00:03:14,440
It is called highway hypnosis.

87
00:03:14,720 --> 00:03:19,360
Experts say your brain drives on autopilot while your mind wanders.

88
00:03:19,600 --> 00:03:21,120
Your mind was not wandering.

89
00:03:21,280 --> 00:03:22,360
It was moved.

90
00:03:22,640 --> 00:03:23,920
One seat to the right.

91
00:03:24,160 --> 00:03:28,600
That is why the passenger seat weighed exactly as much as a person tonight.

92
00:03:28,880 --> 00:03:29,680
It was you.

93
00:03:29,920 --> 00:03:32,760
For the first time, you were awake for the ride.

94
00:03:33,040 --> 00:03:37,140
So if your car ever beeps for the empty passenger seat, don't look.

95
00:03:37,760 --> 00:03:39,920
You might see who has been driving.

96
00:03:40,240 --> 00:03:41,840
Thank you for calling Night Support.

97
00:03:42,080 --> 00:03:43,211
Please drive safely.

98
00:03:43,760 --> 00:03:44,720
Someone has to.
